<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">Frankish Kingdom of Burgundy</h1><p class="st-meta">561 CE – 751 CE (approx.) · capital Chalon-sur-Saône</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Merovingian kingdom of the Rhône and Saône valleys, built on the old Kingdom of the Burgundians and ruled from Chalon-sur-Saône.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/franks">Franks</a> conquered the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-the-burgundians">Kingdom of the Burgundians</a> in 534. At the division of 561 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chlothar-i">Chlothar I's</a> son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guntram">Guntram</a> received <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-burgundy">Burgundy</a> with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orleans">Orléans</a>, ruling from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chalon-sur-saone">Chalon-sur-Saône</a>. The kingdom stretched from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/loire">Loire</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alps">Alps</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guntram">Guntram</a>, a long-reigning king later venerated as a saint, acted as mediator between his feuding brothers' kingdoms. <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-burgundy">Burgundy</a> kept its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-law">Roman law</a> and Gallo-Roman aristocracy and its own mayor of the palace. The Irish monk <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/columbanus">Columbanus</a> founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luxeuil-abbey">Luxeuil</a> there, but was expelled by King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theuderic-ii">Theuderic II</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brunhilda-of-austrasia">Brunhild</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After 613 <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-burgundy">Burgundy</a> was ruled together with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/neustria">Neustria</a> by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chlothar-ii">Chlothar II</a> and his successors, though it kept a separate identity. It passed under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pippinids">Pippinid</a> control, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-martel">Charles Martel</a> subdued it in the 730s. With Pippin's accession in 751 it became a region of the Frankish realm.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/frankish-kingdom-of-burgundy.jpg" alt="Frankish Kingdom of Burgundy" width="320" height="326"><figcaption>Image: PhylémonCyclone · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Les_4_commendement_de_bourgognes.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>561 CE – 751 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Chalon-sur-Saône</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Guntram, Theuderic II</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Latin, Frankish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/france">France</a>, <a href="/countries/switzerland">Switzerland</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Burgundy (Merovingian), Kingdom of Burgundy</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=656&amp;focus=frankish-kingdom-of-burgundy" aria-label="Frankish Kingdom of Burgundy on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4823 588 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Frankish Kingdom of Burgundy lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5143 844L5054 728M5143 844L5143 844"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5054 728h0M5143 844h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5143 844h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5143 844h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=656&amp;focus=frankish-kingdom-of-burgundy">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
